Chapter: OauthIsland
  cites Net chapter OAuthClient
  cites Net chapter OAuthProvider
  cites Trust chapter ExternalAuthBridge

 Compile coverage for three chapters that had none.

 This is the smallest test in the battery and it is the one that closes
 the actual cause. `OAuthClient` had never compiled, and the
 reason nobody knew is that its only citers were `OAuthProvider` and
 `ExternalAuthBridge`, and NOTHING cited those: a dead island of three
 chapters, reachable from no battery run, free to rot. Fixing the
 compile error without giving them a citer would have left them exactly
 as unreachable as before, and the next defect would have gone the same
 way.

 So this file's job is to be cited BY the battery and to cite THEM. It
 asserts almost nothing about behaviour on purpose -- the behaviour is
 not what was broken, and a thin assertion is honest about that where an
 elaborate one would imply a coverage that does not exist. One value is
 read from each chapter so the cite cannot be dead-code-eliminated into
 a no-op.

 What it does prove, every battery run: these three chapters still
 compile, `uri-encode` still resolves for the one that calls it, and
 nobody has re-broken the citation graph.

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("nonce " & (oauth-state-new "abc" "verifier" 1).os-state-nonce)
    print-line-uni ("issuer " & google-issuer)
    print-line-uni ("provider " & (provider-trust-google).pt-provider)
  end
